{"title":"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Similar_to_1,_Less_Math_Jargon)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Similar to 1, Less Math Jargon)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the addition shown below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are distinct digits. How many different values are possible for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43a9d725cbf38b81b4523dbd012ce90bbd022cea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}[t]{r}     ABBCB \\\\ + \\ BCADA \\\\ \\hline     DBDDD \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc8618c844b0added082fc7f6a284ffdda283049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf {(A) } 2 \\qquad \\textbf {(B) } 4 \\qquad \\textbf {(C) } 7 \\qquad \\textbf {(D) } 8 \\qquad \\textbf {(E) } 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note from the addition of the last digits that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5a15ed4ef17391abd446c726ecefad5d70edc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B=D\\text{ or }A+B=D+10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"246\" height=\"14\" />. \nFrom the addition of the frontmost digits, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b831312585cb4ab6697896f86b72accbddbc4b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> cannot have a carry, since the answer is still a five-digit number. Also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> cant have a carry since then for the second column, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2db2dbce80e9bd3677015446f8219625315b3c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C + 1 + D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" /> cant equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. \nTherefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca40b0cad654c5ba05b678aa8eb94dfc972947f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B=D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Using the second or fourth column, this then implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/9/7296755ef63523ef0ed2e997caae100445bbb44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18f4d5b268ed6537f2a5d6123091fc8b34dee09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B+C=B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/2072bfcb168c0254116c78263126d900d7e7c956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C+D=D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />. \nNote that all of the remaining equalities are now satisfied: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34aa64bf491837f5f32a12c1d517e1b5c0ed9a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B=D, B+C=B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"192\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/4440d49041e17db8339cec8b1e5ec8fdf791c752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B+A=D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />. Since the digits must be distinct, the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c43733c628919124fe2d151e501a45f5af62e59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, and the largest possible value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/11697470636f9d6d3a4937d0bee9f814d5fdfa71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\le D\\le9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />, so the number of possible values is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f2fb5b6047f99ed1c6294aca81de10d9877a20e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Similar_to_1.2C_Less_Math_Jargon.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Similar_to_1,_Less_Math_Jargon)\">Solution 2 (Similar to 1, Less Math Jargon)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Similar to 1, Less Math Jargon)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> cannot equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>First, we can easily find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85aac914361efb48aaa13187304c1c5bdfef0589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />. Look at the middle column of the addition problem, which reads <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc98949e3e2ed214cc68e3686786118254de2cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B + C = B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />. The only digit you can add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> without changing its value is zero, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85aac914361efb48aaa13187304c1c5bdfef0589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we can deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b831312585cb4ab6697896f86b72accbddbc4b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be a two-digit number because it would create a carry. Look at the column immediately to the left of the middle one: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f26a645d12e41d279b1be11b15f65c7040e01da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C + D = D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85aac914361efb48aaa13187304c1c5bdfef0589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />, this is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f46d79f986dd37b371164393ab34a4fddb85f592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 + D = D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />. If the column to its right (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />) generated a carry of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, this column would become <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b3e084da1fde3107ceb9f6286404b08389488b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 0 + D = D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" />, which is impossible (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b6108849121218d8caf855180348a5a172c8a44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + D \\neq D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />). Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> cannot carry over; it must be a single digit, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e43500b896047669fb9ba96ec80447ced28011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B = D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Since all digits must be distinct and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85aac914361efb48aaa13187304c1c5bdfef0589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />, the smallest possible non-zero digits we can choose for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fd98f4d430c80047b5c62fcdbda50ebe09325dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B = D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c43733c628919124fe2d151e501a45f5af62e59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must remain a single digit, the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d9714840d9bb2dcfe02d8111ff81df1e71bae25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 - 3 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f2fb5b6047f99ed1c6294aca81de10d9877a20e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288#Created_Pages\" title=\"User：Icosahedron0288\">Icosahedron0288</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/x5e1DJSXFss\">https://youtu.be/x5e1DJSXFss</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/CCOjtLn2AKM\">https://youtu.be/CCOjtLn2AKM</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wiki